    {
      "id": "claim_bcf939a909bf4b5b988559671c2df5ea",
      "statement": "`make_git_repo` writes sample files (optionally including an existing `openwiki/` or `.openwiki/` wiki with `.claims/`, `index.md` and `.last-update.json`) and commits them, skipping when `git` is unavailable; `make_remote_repo` returns a bare origin that accepts pushes, or with `bare=False` a non-bare seed with the branch checked out so `git` refuses the push, which is how real push failures are produced.",
